<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-3.6.xsd">

    <!--
      The demo application's own schema, on its own line.

      Registered as a LiquibaseMasterChangeLogLocation bean, which Valtimo's LiquibaseRunner runs
      once per location. Valtimo's own changelogs are separate runs; this file never includes or
      modifies them, and its changesets are identified by this path, so neither can affect the
      other. Nothing is added to Valtimo's files.

      Why the demo owns this at all: the *plugin* stores nothing and needs no database changes to
      install, which is a property worth keeping — an operator can drop the jar in and take it out
      again. Durable document storage is a host concern, and a real installation points Valtimo at
      the Documenten API or S3. The demo has neither, so it provides the smallest stand-in.
    -->
    <include file="epistola-demo/0001-stored-document.xml" relativeToChangelogFile="true"/>

</databaseChangeLog>
